  ok: the M mode context is 0, 1, 3, 5, 7 for harts 0 to 4
  ok: enable, threshold and claim addresses of every hart are the PAC's
  ok: the source is enabled in the PLIC context of this hart
  ok: and in no other context (QEMU: clear after reset)
  ok: the priority of the source is the ceiling of its handler
  ok: outside a protected object the threshold of this hart is 0
  ok: inside it the threshold is the ceiling
  ok: generated names are PLIC source numbers, Interrupt_ID is 1 to 186
  ok: 0 and 187 are not an Interrupt_ID, 1, 90, 117 and 186 are
  ok: the interrupt priorities are PLIC levels 1 to 7, task priorities 0
  ok: the threshold of this hart is the level of the set priority
  ok: the handler took in as many bytes as console.in has
  ok: the bytes are those of console.in, in order
  ok: the source is not pending after the handler
  ok: msip of this hart reads set
  ok: and clear after Clear_MSIP
  ok: mtime runs
  ok: the mtimecmp of the other harts is untouched (QEMU: 0 after reset)
